==Strategy==
{{Lineup
|Roe Cat|40
|Sashimi Cat
|?
|?
|?
|Slime Cat|40
|Can Can Cat|40
|Fishman Cat|40
|Courier Cat|40
|Awakened Bahamut Cat|30
|talent10 = Explosion Lv10
|cannon = Thunderbolt
|notes = *Fill the first row with the best Starting Money, Starting Level or Attack combos you have. However, it's best if you have Sashimi Cat since Roe Cat in the combo can serve as a tanker too.
*If you feel like you don't have enough damage output, you can use a rich cat on the last stages and swap out some of the combos.
}}

Send Slime Cat immediately to have it trade with Aku Doge, then send Can Can Cat, Courier Cat and Fishman Cat in order so that they enter Gilgamesh's blindspot together. After that try to spawn Awakened Bahamut Cat as soon as possible (just don't have it caught in Gilgamesh's attack), and spam the bottom row plus at least 1 Roe Cat, more if you have extra cash. Slime Cat will need a bit of timing, but Can Can Cat, Fisherman Cat and Courier Cat will usually enter alive even if hit.
Gilgamesh should be dead by the time or very shortly after Lancer arrives. It's crucial to not have Awakened Bahamut Cat hit by any of the peons, as it will survive 2 hits from Lancer at full HP and you need every bit of that time. Now it's a matter of destroying the base before Rider spawns and kills your stack. Lancer deals relatively low damage, and your courier stack can survive 1 hit. Use Thunderbolt to buy time if necessary and knockback Lancer quickly. Once Lancer is behind the base, the Roe Cat from earlier can safely tank the hits and let you finish the base. Even if Rider spawns and attacks, it's not the end of the world if the enemy base is already quite low, as more Courier Cats can do a little bit of chip damage under the protection of Roe Cats.

